      "text": "VT-7\nEAGLES\nCDR Thomas L. Kellner NAS MERIDIAN, MISSISSIPPI CDR Adam J. Fisel\nCommanding Officer Executive Officer\nSunday, 29-Nov-2026\nSUNRISE: 06:39 MOONRISE: 22:32 ILLUM: 72% JULIAN DATE: 6333\nSUNSET: 16:49 MOONSET: 11:25\nTOTAL FLY EVENTS: 0 TOTAL FLY HRS: 0.0 SYL FLY EVENTS: 0 SYL FLY HRS: 0.0\nTOTAL SIM EVENTS: 0 TOTAL SIM HRS: 0.0 SYL SIM EVENTS: 0 SYL SIM HRS: 0.0\nQuestions:\nEP Question: T/F AUTO RETRACTION (BLOWBACK) OF THE FLAPS BEGINS AT APPROXIMATELY 200 KNOTS.\nTHE OBOGS HEAT EXCHANGER: A. REDUCES THE TEMPERATURE OF ENGINE BLEED AIR. B. REDUCES THE PRESSURE OF ENGINE\nNATOPS: BLEED AIR. C. ANALYZES THE TEMPERATURE OF BLEED AIR THAT HAS PASSED THROUGH THE OXYGEN CONCENTRATOR. D.\nABSORBS CONTAMINANTS THROUGH MOLECULAR SIEVES.\nSOP: HOW IS CROSSWIND CALCULATED WHEN THERE IS A GUST COMPONENT?\nDUTY/WATCH ASSIGNED SIGN IN SIGN OUT\nODO (ON CALL) NORTON, OWEN T, 1stLt 0000 2359\nDUTY DRIVER SCOBY, NATHANIAL D, ENS 0000 1600\nIWO FALLON, MILO, LTJG 0600 1800\nIWO HOLAVA, JACOB, ENS 1800 0600\nCOMMENTS:\nNMM: CLOSED\nNJW: CLOSED\nR-4404: CLOSED\nAREA 1/2/3/4: CLOSED\nMERIDIAN 2 MOA: CLOSED\nAF USING BHAM MOA: NONE\nAF USING SEARAY: NONE\nAF USING PINE HILLS/CAMDEN RIDGE: NONE\nVT-7 FCLP: NMM: NONE; NJW: NONE\nVT-9 FCLP: NMM: NONE; NJW: NONE\nRESERVISTS ON ACTIVE DUTY: NONE\nRESERVISTS DRILLING: NONE\n***MISSION COMMANDERS ASSIGNED IAW SOP***\nR/S: 0; W/U: 0; FITU: 0\nADVANCING X\u2019s: 0\nSIT: 63\nUPCOMING OPS:\n2 DEC: ROBD / IGS\n11 DEC: HOLIDAY PARTY\n12 DEC: CHILDREN\u2019S HOLIDAY PARTY\n22 JAN: WINGING"
